---
// <BcnPlanItemsTable> — the plan's items as a table you can edit (2026-10-28, the SOW review: "edit records in a table
// view rather than row by row"), beside the Gantt on the Schedule tab (Show As: Chart or Table). Name, Level, Start, End,
// Date Type, Milestone, Owners and Notes, one row per item in outline order. In your draft the editable cells are
// white with the brand edge, as the budget sheet's; the rest read. The runtime is ./plan-items-table.ts.
//
// bcn-lego-checked: the table IS AG Grid community on the spoke's Beacon theme (src/lib/beacon-grid.ts), as the budget
// sheet and Beacon's grids are; its editors are AG Grid's. No esa- lego is an editable grid. The CSS is the cell states.
---

<div class="bcn-pit" data-bcn-plan-items-table>
  <p class="bcn-pit__hint typography-body-sm" data-pit-hint>Double-click a cell, or type, to change it; paste a block from a spreadsheet across cells. Each change goes to your draft.</p>
  <div class="bcn-pit__grid" data-pit-grid></div>
</div>

<style>
  .bcn-pit { display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
  .bcn-pit__hint { margin: 0; padding: var(--spacing-200) var(--spacing-400); color: var(--color-content-default-secondary); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-border-default); }
  .bcn-pit:not([data-editable]) .bcn-pit__hint { display: none; }
  .bcn-pit__grid { inline-size: 100%; }
  .bcn-pit :global(.bcn-pit__parent) { font-weight: var(--typography-font-weight-semibold); }
  .bcn-pit[data-editable] :global(.bcn-pit__edit) { background: var(--color-background-elevation-raised); box-shadow: inset 0 -1px 0 color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-background-brand) 40%, transparent); }
  .bcn-pit[data-editable] :global(.bcn-pit__read) { background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-content-default) 5%, var(--color-background-elevation-raised)); color: var(--color-content-default-secondary); }
</style>
